  "body": "For the [Badging API](https://w3c.github.io/badging/), it would be helpful if there was an opaque means to identify that a web application has been \"installed\". \r\n\r\nLooking for guidance on this... but I'm wondering if we could add a \"appId\" to the \"environment\" (or the \"environment settings object\"), which would be either `null` (not installed) or the URL [identify](https://www.w3.org/TR/appmanifest/#dfn-identity) of the Installed Web Application. \r\n\r\nThat way, a spec editor can check if the application has an explicit installed identity, and make decisions based on that. If an application is installed or not wouldn't be directly exposed to developers.  \r\n\r\nThis is roughly how I'd like to use `[=environment/appId=]`:\r\n\r\n1. Let |appId| be the environment's [=environment/appId=]. \r\n2. If |appId| is `null`, return ....\r\n3. Let |badge| be the [=badge=] associated with the [=installed web application=] |appId|.\r\n4. In parallel, set |badge| to |value|...\r\n\r\n",
